      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T02:27:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So what are all the futex commands that could cause a wakeup? And how many of them wake up more than 1 thread?",
      "parentUuid": "112dbd9c_2d802d5e",
      "revId": "1060ce97cd18de5bc2436f825abef0d4b69a5dc7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f321514_f9cba5d1",
        "filename": "include/uapi/linux/futex.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 1934715
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T18:12:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe the following ones can cause a wake up:\n-FUTEX_WAKE\n-FUTEX_REQUEUE\n-FUTEX_CMP_REQUEUE\n-FUTEX_WAKE_OP\n-FUTEX_WAKE_BITSET\n-FUTEX_CMP_REQUEUE_PI\n\nThe number of threads that they can wake up is conveyed through the val parameter in the futex syscall signature:\n\n  long syscall(SYS_futex, uint32_t *uaddr, int futex_op, uint32_t val,\n                    const struct timespec *timeout,   /* or: uint32_t val2 */\n                    uint32_t *uaddr2, uint32_t val3);\n                    \nfrom https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/futex.2.html",
      "parentUuid": "1f51458c_fe479f6d",
      "revId": "1060ce97cd18de5bc2436f825abef0d4b69a5dc7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
